    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/4/44607.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 5,
    "turn_text": "I can tell you that there's no district in America that produces more milk, nor more meth than the 21st Congressional District. We're the top agricultural district in the top agricultural state, but we're also one of the most economically challenged There was a study done some time ago some of the listeners may know about it the measure of America that was originally done on my oxfam And I think it was 2010 2012, but it reflected that the 21st congressional was actually the poorest congressional district in America when he took a look at health care life expectancy educational attainment in power derates and so it's certainly a district that has a lot of challenges, but it's a It's such a fantastic district, and as you know, the fantastic communities, the Fire, Blossom, and Dotas, the Delano's, the McFarland's of the world. Many of you may have seen that movie, McFarland USA. And if you haven't, please see that, Kevin Costner. But that is such a great reflection of the grit, the community, and the heart of the hardworking families here in the 21st.",
