  {
    "episode_id": 44607,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/4/44607.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 8,
    "turn_text": "It's an issue of the public charge that has really affected some of the HIV activists nationally who are concerned both about how the administration is impacting access to HIV services. But what this could potentially mean when we have the huge International AIDS Conference in the Bay Area next year. I wanted to just share a story with you from my day as an election monitor. I was in Kern County. in a church that was acting as a polling station. And I learned a really important lesson about being a US citizen. And I had been a citizen then for about six, seven months. And it's really not about birth, but about values. A recently naturalized Yemeni couple who spoke really next to no English came into the hall to cast their vote. And I was just blown away by how the entire staff Many of them, and you never want to make assumptions, but nonetheless, they appeared. How shall I put this on the other side? But they made every effort, every extra mile to help them vote. The woman was pregnant, she needed to sit down, needed a glass of water. And to my surprise, after they cast their ballots, everyone broke into applause. The polling manager with, again, how shall I put this, her higher the hair, closer to heaven hair. She came up to me afterwards and said, Lord help me, those citizens were going to vote. So that really deeply affected me. And I think that's your constituency. Do you see much of that, a sort of a ground up bipartisanship?",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "Being a U.S. citizen is defined more by shared values than by place of birth.",
        "confidence": 0.96
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker served as an election monitor in Kern County at a church used as a polling station.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "A recently naturalized Yemeni couple with limited English proficiency voted at the polling station.",
        "confidence": 0.93
