  {
    "episode_id": 44607,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/4/44607.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 9,
    "turn_text": "Very, very much so. And if there was one thing, I think this administration might have had is really activating a lot of these citizens. And the people that were eligible for citizenship or if they were recently a naturalized citizen to go out there and cast that vote for the first time. We met a number of people just canvassing that would come up and say, You know, I've never voted before, but now I'm going to vote for you. And there's nothing more meaningful than that. Every time that anybody ever told me that, it literally gave me chills. And I'm just so proud to be able to represent hardworking individuals and families like that.",
