  {
    "episode_id": 44607,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/4/44607.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 14,
    "turn_text": "Absolutely. And one of my heroes is Nye Bevan, the first Minister of Health of the UK after the Second World War, who brought the National Health Service to the UK. But many of my progressive friends roll their eyes when I say, all we need to do is recreate the National Health Service here. And I suppose another way of approaching the question is to ask you, what are the distinctly American ways that you believe health can be brought to everybody?",
