  },
  {
    "episode_id": 44607,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/4/44607.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 17,
    "turn_text": "It's absolutely a women's health issue. Women's health issues should not be excluded from the range of services that are provided to every citizen. Those are decisions that should be made between a woman and a darker. Certainly, the base fundamental of that is to protect individual rights with the things that we all know. People should have and be afforded. And certainly it's those types of rights. But the idea about being able to provide, you know, contraceptive and these types of things over the counter are absolutely something that we ought to be doing. And you might have seen some of the legislation that we're being put forward today with respect to that.",
