    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/4/44607.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 19,
    "turn_text": "Well, the idea of the over-utilization of antibiotics in the meat industry, absolute concern. But it's an absolute opportunity, too. It goes to one, to look at the industry and why. why is it necessary to use all these antibiotics, right? And so what can we be doing to improve that landscape where animals aren't getting sick? Number one, but two, it's such a nice opportunity, you know, for more industry research to be able to develop different things, you know, so that they aren't using antibiotics in the first place. And that's, you know, that's something that also, we were just having hearings on this and it might be a little esoteric, but is that the Department of Ag is trying to decentralize a lot of their technological expertise by moving the National Institute for Food and Ag Research, NIFA, and the ERS, their economic research services out of DC to watch to Kansas City. Well, when you're talking about something like NIFA, Well, they're able to coordinate and collaborate and work together with something called NIH, right, right here in DC. So you have this concentration of experts, right, that really can work together. They could, once I said, once I get this, collaborate on better, better programming, therapies, technology, and so on. And this decentralized decentralization is really an unfortunate step in the wrong direction with regard to that.",
