  {
    "episode_id": 44607,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/4/44607.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 20,
    "turn_text": "Well, absolutely, because the scientific community has to speak, engage, and learn from each other. And there are a number of areas across the NIH and CDC where it's not just this administration, but administrations have, particularly this one, has try and restricted the way scientists talk to each other. I wanted also to ask you about your support for global health. You've been a very vocal supporter of sustained US support for the Global Fund to fight AIDS, TB and malaria. And why have you done that? Why is global health important to you?",
