    "turn_idx": 22,
    "turn_text": "Absolutely. I mean, you'll remember that I used to work for the late ambassador, Richard Holbrook, a sort of anti-Trump when it comes to foreign policy. And, you know, his understanding that the investment in a Zambian copper mine worker was crucial to the safety of an agricultural worker in Delano, for example. And that overseas development is as much a tool of American power as the military and sanctions. So you guys have in the House of Representatives have passed the legislation needed to fund the next replenishment of the Global Fund. It's now with the Senate. Fingers crossed it's looking good. We never take anything for granted. But what can you do? And what would you recommend that we do to get the Senate to get funding for the Global Fund over the fence?",
