  {
    "episode_id": 44607,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/4/44607.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 24,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, and we're not going to let him. Just one last question on global health. And I suppose this does get a bit wonky now. One of the things I'm very interested in doing is seeing how different academic disciplines affect public health. And you were an engineer. You worked internationally, as you said. From those experiences, how do you feel they can inform health care? You know, as an engineer, rather than a public health specialist, how do we prioritize responses to future threats? And sure, there's epidemics like Ebola. But what about non-communicable diseases like COPD or diabetes?",
