    "turn_text": "It's just a quality for all. I may have related this story about why I'm a U.S. Congressman today. And sure, I've done a lot of business things. I've created health care clinics, as you've said. I've created jobs. I've tried to make a difference in the community. But really what drives me more than anything else is a sense of social justice. My mom was one of the state of Nevada's first equal opportunity officers. My grandmother, back in the Philippines in Manila, took it upon herself to open the first and only social club for African-American troops. So when I see anybody being discriminated against, brothers and sisters, sons and daughters that aren't being afforded the rights, the criticism, their respect that they deserve, it's just something that I need to stand up for.",
