    "turn_text": "that we're doing all that we can certainly in this office that we're doing all like we can't you may know that we recently passed the equality act right which is a huge step forward and certainly something else that can be brought before the Senate, Mr. McConnell's office. And, you know, the things that we've been trying to do myself personally is fund clinics that may address some specialty issues that are among the LGBTQ community. And, you know, just to fight back and to stand up, you know, this administration's ban on transgender service people. I mean, that is just disgraceful. But early on a couple years ago, I had an opportunity to go to a Remembrance Day of at Stan State in Turlock. And this young woman there, she told the most powerful story about her transformation. I still think about it today. And she was telling us the story is that she had certainly a number of issues in that she considered taking her own life. And she was going to go step in front of a train. And she tells the story is the funny thing is that she said she was just, you know, praying for something to give her a sign. And while she was trying to get up on the track, she tripped on her high hill and fell down the bank. But then she took that as a sign. and is such a great activist and an example of being such a fine individual that serve our community. And so it was great that my whole family went, my two younger boys went and She really just made such an impression on me that, once again, to stand up for individuals like this is something I'm proud to do each and every day.",
